# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #fields: no shadowing by depth inside one activation; #method-parts: call: code code takes
# the general path): under call: S S the int: y 5 of the if body assigns the one place y, the root y of S as data (a
# declaration inside the if body is not a root head of the data, and S has one place y). The read after the if sees
# 5, and 5 is published into S. A route that lowers call: S S onto the one-operand form keeps a second y in the if
# body: seen and S\y stay 1. Entry 7.
int: seen 0
S:
    int: y 1
    if: y = 1
        int: y 5
    node\seen: y
end: S
fn: unit_seen () int
    return: node\seen
end: unit_seen
call: S S
int: ok 81
if: S\y = 5 && unit_seen() = 5
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
